HTML\":{\"__html\":\"Germanic and Norse cultures prized strength above all. <strong>Bernard</strong> means 'brave as a bear' — perfect for large, protective dogs like {bernese-mountain-dog}s. <strong>Conrad</strong> means 'bold counsel,' and <strong>Gerard</strong> means 'spear strength.' <strong>Magnus</strong> literally means 'great' in Latin but was widely used by Scandinavian royalty.\"}}]\n29:[\"$\",\"p\",\"7\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Viking-age strength names: <strong>Ragnar</strong> (warrior), <strong>Bjorn</strong> (bear), <strong>Ulf</strong> (wolf), <strong>Sigurd</strong> (victory guardian), <strong>Astrid</strong> (divinely beautiful and strong). For a modern twist, the Old Norse <strong>Thrym</strong> (thunder, noise) creates a unique and powerful name. <strong>Brunhilde</strong> (armored warrior woman) and <strong>Siegfried</strong> (victory peace) carry Wagnerian grandeur.\"}}]\n2a:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"8\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Asian Names Meaning Strength 🌏\"]}]\n2b:[\"$\",\"p\",\"9\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Asian languages offer subtle, profound strength names. Japanese <strong>Ken</strong> (strong, healthy), <strong>Isamu</strong> (courage, bravery), <strong>Takeshi</strong> (warrior, fierce), <strong>Tsuyoshi</strong> (strong). Chinese <strong>Li</strong> (strength, power), <strong>Qiang</strong> (strong, powerful), <strong>Yong</strong> (brave, courageous). Korean <strong>Yong</strong> (dragon, brave) and <strong>Dae</strong> (great, big).\"}}]\n2c:[\"$\",\"p\",\"10\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Sanskrit-derived strength names from India: <strong>Bala</strong> (strength), <strong>Veer/Vir</strong> (brave, heroic), <strong>Shakti</strong> (power, energy), <strong>Tejas</strong> (brilliance, power). These names carry spiritual depth alongside strength, making them meaningful choices for deeply bonded pets.\"}}]\n2d:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"11\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Nature-Inspired Strength Names 🌳\"]}]\n2e:[\"$\",\"p\",\"12\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Nature provides endless symbols of strength. <strong>Oakley/Oak</strong> from the mighty oak tree. <strong>Stone</strong>, <strong>Flint</strong>, <strong>Granite</strong> from unyielding rock. <strong>Steel</strong>, <strong>Iron</strong>, <strong>Titanium</strong> from metals. Animal-inspired strength: <strong>Bear</strong>, <strong>Lion</strong>, <strong>Tiger</strong>, <strong>Wolf</strong>, <strong>Hawk</strong>, <strong>Eagle</strong>, <strong>Bull</strong>, <strong>Gorilla</strong>.\"}}]\n2f:[\"$\",\"p\",\"13\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Weather phenomena bring dramatic strength: <strong>Storm</strong>, <strong>Thunder</strong>, <strong>Lightning</strong>, <strong>Cyclone</strong>, <strong>Avalanche</strong>, <strong>Tsunami</strong>, <strong>Quake</strong>. Mountain names evoke enduring power: <strong>Everest</strong>, <strong>Rocky</strong>, <strong>Summit</strong>, <strong>Ridge</strong>, <strong>Peak</strong>. For a more subtle strength, try <strong>River</strong> (relentless) or <strong>Cedar</strong> (tall and enduring).\"}}]\n30:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"14\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Warrior & Hero Strength Names 🛡️\"]}]\n31:[\"$\",\"p\",\"15\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Historical warriors and heroes provide some of the strongest name inspirations. <strong>Samson</strong> (biblical strongman), <strong>Achilles</strong> (Greek hero), <strong>Arthur</strong> (legendary king), <strong>Boudica</strong> (Celtic warrior queen), <strong>Leonidas</strong> (Spartan king), <strong>Alexander</strong> (conqueror).\"}}]\n32:[\"$\",\"p\",\"16\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Modern heroes: <strong>Ali</strong> (the Greatest), <strong>Tyson</strong> (Iron Mike), <strong>Diana</strong> (Wonder Woman), <strong>Thor</strong> (Marvel's god of thunder), <strong>Xena</strong> (warrior princess), <strong>Mulan</strong> (warrior woman). The name <strong>Brienne</strong> (from Game of Thrones) and <strong>Katniss</strong> (from Hunger Games) bring fictional warrior spirit.\"}}]\n33:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"❓ Frequently Asked Questions\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"details\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Will a 'strong' name make my pet aggressive?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"No — a name does not determine behavior. A strong name simply reflects the respect and admiration you have for your pet's character. Many of the gentlest pets have the mightiest names.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"What if my pet is small? Can I still use a strong name?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Small pets with big names create the most delightful contrast. A tiny chihuahua named Titan or a hamster named Goliath is instantly memorable and charming. Strength isn't about size.\"}]]}],[\"$\",