\"$\",\"$L4\",null,{\"parallelRouterKey\":\"children\",\"error\":\"$undefined\",\"errorStyles\":\"$undefined\",\"errorScripts\":\"$undefined\",\"template\":[\"$\",\"$L5\",null,{}],\"templateStyles\":\"$undefined\",\"templateScripts\":\"$undefined\",\"notFound\":\"$undefined\",\"forbidden\":\"$undefined\",\"unauthorized\":\"$undefined\"}]]}]\ne:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L4\",null,{\"parallelRouterKey\":\"children\",\"error\":\"$undefined\",\"errorStyles\":\"$undefined\",\"errorScripts\":\"$undefined\",\"template\":[\"$\",\"$L5\",null,{}],\"templateStyles\":\"$undefined\",\"templateScripts\":\"$undefined\",\"notFound\":\"$undefined\",\"forbidden\":\"$undefined\",\"unauthorized\":\"$undefined\"}]]}]\nf:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[\"$L14\",null,[\"$\",\"$L15\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$16\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.MetadataOutlet\",\"children\":\"$@17\"}]}]]}]\n18:[]\n10:\"$W18\"\n11:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"h\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L19\",null,{\"children\":\"$L1a\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"hidden\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L1b\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$16\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.Metadata\",\"children\":\"$L1c\"}]}]}],null]}]\n13:[\"$\",\"link\",\"0\",{\"rel\":\"stylesheet\",\"href\":\"/_next/static/chunks/0_novvjei_gxi.css\",\"precedence\":\"next\",\"crossOrigin\":\"$undefined\",\"nonce\":\"$undefined\"}]\n1d:T159a,{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BlogPosting\",\"headline\":\"Animal Names That Mean Strength: Powerful Names for Mighty Pets 💪\",\"description\":\"Give your pet a name that embodies power, courage, and resilience. Discover 150+ animal names that mean strength from languages and cultures around the world.\",\"datePublished\":\"2026-06-16\",\"dateModified\":\"2026-07-06\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"BestAnimalNames Editorial Team\",\"url\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com/about/\"},\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"BestAnimalNames\",\"url\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com\"},\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com/blog/animal-names-that-mean-strength/\"},\"wordCount\":458,\"articleBody\":\" A name that means 'strength' gives your pet an identity of power and resilience from day one. Whether you have a muscular {dog}, a fierce {cat}, or a tiny pet with an enormous personality, a strong name sets the right tone. This guide explores names that literally mean strength, power, and courage across world languages. Greek & Latin Strength Names 🏛️ The classical languages give us some of the most enduring strength names. <strong>Valentina/Valentino</strong> (from Latin 'valens' meaning strong, healthy) works beautifully for a pet with a robust constitution. <strong>Ethan</strong> (Hebrew origin, meaning firm, strong) has been popular for decades. <strong>Andrea</strong> (from Greek 'andreia' meaning courage, strength) brings classical elegance. Direct Latin strength names: <strong>Fortis</strong> (strong), <strong>Valens</strong> (healthy, strong), <strong>Robur</strong> (oak, strength), <strong>Virtus</strong> (valor). Greek options: <strong>Kratos</strong> (power, strength), <strong>Bia</strong> (force), <strong>Alke</strong> (prowess, courage), <strong>Dynamis</strong> (power). For historical resonance, <strong>Spartacus</strong>, <strong>Caesar</strong>, <strong>Augustus</strong> bring Roman might. Norse & Germanic Power Names ⚔️ Germanic and Norse cultures prized strength above all. <strong>Bernard</strong> means 'brave as a bear' — perfect for large, protective dogs like {bernese-mountain-dog}s. <strong>Conrad</strong> means 'bold counsel,' and <strong>Gerard</strong> means 'spear strength.' <strong>Magnus</strong> literally means 'great' in Latin but was widely used by Scandinavian royalty. Viking-age strength names: <strong>Ragnar</strong> (warrior), <strong>Bjorn</strong> (bear), <strong>Ulf</strong> (wolf), <strong>Sigurd</strong> (victory guardian), <strong>Astrid</strong> (divinely beautiful and strong). For a modern twist, the Old Norse <strong>Thrym</strong> (thunder, noise) creates a unique and powerful name. <strong>Brunhilde</strong> (armored warrior woman) and <strong>Siegfried</strong> (victory peace) carry Wagnerian grandeur. Asian Names Meaning Strength 🌏 Asian languages offer subtle, profound strength names. Japanese <strong>Ken</strong> (strong, healthy), <strong>Isamu</strong> (courage, bravery), <strong>Takeshi</strong> (warrior, fierce), <strong>Tsuyoshi</strong> (strong). Chinese <strong>Li</strong> (strength, power), <strong>Qiang</strong> (strong, powerful), <strong>Yong</strong> (brave, courageous). Korean <strong>Yong</strong> (dragon, brave) and <strong>Dae</strong> (great, big). Sanskrit-derived strength names from India: <strong>Bala</strong> (strength), <strong>Veer/Vir</strong> (brave, heroic), <strong>Shakti</strong> (power, energy), <strong>Tejas</strong> (brilliance, power). These names carry spiritual depth alongside strength, making them meaningful choices for deeply bonded pets. Nature-Inspired Strength Names 🌳 Nature provides endless symbols of strength. <strong>Oakley/Oak</strong> from the mighty oak tree. <strong>Stone</strong>, <strong>Flint</strong>, <strong>Granite</strong> from unyielding rock. <strong>Steel</strong>, <strong>Iron</strong>, <strong>Titanium</strong> from metals. Animal-inspired strength: <strong>Bear</strong>, <strong>Lion</strong>, <strong>Tiger</strong>, <strong>Wolf</strong>, <strong>Hawk</strong>, <strong>Eagle</strong>, <strong>Bull</strong>, <strong>Gorilla</strong>. Weather phenomena bring dramatic strength: <strong>Storm</strong>, <strong>Thunder</strong>, <strong>Lightning</strong>, <strong>Cyclone</strong>, <strong>Avalanche</strong>, <strong>Tsunami</strong>, <strong>Quake</strong>. Mountain names evoke enduring power: <strong>Everest</strong>, <strong>Rocky</strong>, <strong>Summit</strong>, <strong>Ridge</strong>, <strong>Peak</strong>. For a more subtle strength, try <strong>River</strong> (relentless) or <strong>Cedar</strong> (tall and enduring). Warrior & Hero Strength Names 🛡️ Historical warriors and heroes provide some of the strongest name inspirations. <strong>Samson</strong> (biblical strongman), <strong>Achilles</strong> (Greek hero), <strong>Arthur</strong> (legendary king), <strong>Boudica</strong> (Celtic warrior queen), <strong>Leonidas</strong> (Spartan king), <strong>Alexander</strong> (conqueror). Modern heroes: <strong>Ali</strong> (the Greatest), <strong>Tyson</strong> (Iron Mike), <strong>Diana</strong> (Wonder Woman), <strong>Thor</strong> (Marvel's god of thunder), <strong>Xena</strong> (warrior princess), <strong>Mulan</strong> (warrior woman). The name <strong>Brienne</strong> (from Game of Thrones) and <strong>Katniss</strong> (from Hunger Games) bring fictional warrior spirit.\",\"image\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com/images/og/blog-animal-names-that-mean-strength.png\",\"inLanguage\":\"en\"}14:[[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$1d\"}}],\"$L1e\",\"$L1f\",\"$L20\",\"$L21\"]\n22:T510,{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Will a 'strong' name make my pet aggressive?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"No — a name does not determine behavior. A strong name simply reflects the respect and admiration you have for your pet's character. Many of the gentlest pets have the mightiest names.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What if my pet is small? Can I still use a strong name?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Small pets with big names create the most delightful contrast. A tiny chihuahua named Titan or a hamster named Goliath is instantly memorable and charming. Strength isn't about size.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Should I pick a name whose meaning I can explain to others?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Having a story behind your pet's name adds richness to your bond and makes great conversation. But the most important thing is that you love the sound and feel of the name.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Are names meaning 'strength' more suited to male pets?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Absolutely not. Female strength names like Valentina, Boudica, Athena, Brienne, and Xena are powerful and beautiful. Strength is a universal quality regardless of gender.\"}}]}1e:[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$22\"}}]\n1f:[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"{\\\"@context\\\":\\\"https://schema.org\\\",\\\"@type\\\":\\\"BreadcrumbList\\\",\\\"itemListElement\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":1,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Home\\\",\\\"item\\\":\\\"https://bestanimalnames.com/\\\"},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":2,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Blog\\\",\\\"item\\\":\\\"https://bestanimalnames.com/blog/\\\"},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":3,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Animal Names That Mean Strength: Powerful Names for Mighty Pets 💪\\\",\\\"item\\\":\\\"https://bestanimalnames.com/blog/animal-names-that-mean-strength/\\\"}]}\"}}]\n20:[\"$\",\"nav\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 py-3 text-sm text-gray-500 flex gap-1 flex-wrap\",\"aria-label\":\"Breadcrumb\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{\"href\":\"/\",\"className\":\"hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Home\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"/\"}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{\"href\":\"/blog/\",\"className\":\"hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Blog\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"/\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-800 font-medium\",\"children\":\"Animal Names That Mean Strength: Powerful Names for Mighty Pets 💪\"}]]}]\n21:[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-center mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-6xl mb-4\",\"children\":\"💪\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center justify-center gap-2 text-xs text-gray-500 mb-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-primary/10 text-primary font-semibold px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"Naming Tips\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"2026-06-16\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-gray-500\",\"children\":\"By BestAnimalNames Editorial Team\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"h1\",null,{\"className\":\"text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-4\",\"children\":\"Animal Names That Mean Strength: Powerful Names for Mighty Pets 💪\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-lg text-gray-600 max-w-2xl mx-auto\",\"children\":\"Give your pet a name that embodies power, courage, and resilience. Discover 150+ animal names that mean strength from languages and cultures around the world.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-2 mt-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",\"strong names\",{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-gray-100 text-gray-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"strong names\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"powerful names\",{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-gray-100 text-gray-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"powerful names\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"strength names\",{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-gray-100 text-gray-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"strength names\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"warrior names\",{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-gray-100 text-gray-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"warrior names\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"mighty pet names\",{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-gray-100 text-gray-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"mighty pet names\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"prose prose-lg max-w-none\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"bg-gradient-to-br from-primary/5 to-indigo-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-primary/10 mb-8\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-lg font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\",\"children\":\"📋 Table of Contents\"}],[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-2 list-none pl-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[1,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#greek-latin\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Greek & Latin Strength Names\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[2,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#norse-germanic\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Norse & Germanic Power Names\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[3,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#asian\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Asian Names Meaning Strength\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[4,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#nature\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Nature-Inspired Strength Names\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[5,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#warriors\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Warrior & Hero Strength Names\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[6,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#faq\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"FAQ\"}]]}]]}]]}],\"$L23\",\"$L24\",\"$L25\",\"$L26\",\"$L27\",\"$L28\",\"$L29\",\"$L2a\",\"$L2b\",\"$L2c\",\"$L2d\",\"$L2e\",\"$L2f\",\"$L30\",\"$L31\",\"$L32\"]}],\"$L33\",\"$L34\",\"$L35\",\"$L36\",\"$L37\",\"$L38\"]}]\n23:[\"$\",\"p\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"A name that means 'strength' gives your pet an identity of power and resilience from day one. Whether you have a muscular \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"122\",{\"href\":\"/animal/dog/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Dog\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", a fierce \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"138\",{\"href\":\"/animal/cat/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Cat\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", or a tiny pet with an enormous personality, a strong name sets the right tone. This guide explores names that literally mean strength, power, and courage across world languages.\"]}]\n24:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Greek & Latin Strength Names 🏛️\"]}]\n25:[\"$\",\"p\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"The classical languages give us some of the most enduring strength names. <strong>Valentina/Valentino</strong> (from Latin 'valens' meaning strong, healthy) works beautifully for a pet with a robust constitution. <strong>Ethan</strong> (Hebrew origin, meaning firm, strong) has been popular for decades. <strong>Andrea</strong> (from Greek 'andreia' meaning courage, strength) brings classical elegance.\"}}]\n26:[\"$\",\"p\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Direct Latin strength names: <strong>Fortis</strong> (strong), <strong>Valens</strong> (healthy, strong), <strong>Robur</strong> (oak, strength), <strong>Virtus</strong> (valor). Greek options: <strong>Kratos</strong> (power, strength), <strong>Bia</strong> (force), <strong>Alke</strong> (prowess, courage), <strong>Dynamis</strong> (power). For historical resonance, <strong>Spartacus</strong>, <strong>Caesar</strong>, <strong>Augustus</strong> bring Roman might.\"}}]\n27:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Norse & Germanic Power Names ⚔️\"]}]\n28:[\"$\",\"p\",\"6\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Germanic and Norse cultures prized strength above all. <strong>Bernard</strong> means 'brave as a bear' — perfect for large, protective dogs like {bernese-mountain-dog}s. <strong>Conrad</strong> means 'bold counsel,' and <strong>Gerard</strong> means 'spear strength.' <strong>Magnus</strong> literally means 'great' in Latin but was widely used by Scandinavian royalty.\"}}]\n29:[\"$\",\"p\",\"7\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Viking-age strength names: <strong>Ragnar</strong> (warrior), <strong>Bjorn</strong> (bear), <strong>Ulf</strong> (wolf), <strong>Sigurd</strong> (victory guardian), <strong>Astrid</strong> (divinely beautiful and strong). For a modern twist, the Old Norse <strong>Thrym</strong> (thunder, noise) creates a unique and powerful name. <strong>Brunhilde</strong> (armored warrior woman) and <strong>Siegfried</strong> (victory peace) carry Wagnerian grandeur.\"}}]\n2a:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"8\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Asian Names Meaning Strength 🌏\"]}]\n2b:[\"$\",\"p\",\"9\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Asian languages offer subtle, profound strength names. Japanese <strong>Ken</strong> (strong, healthy), <strong>Isamu</strong> (courage, bravery), <strong>Takeshi</strong> (warrior, fierce), <strong>Tsuyoshi</strong> (strong). Chinese <strong>Li</strong> (strength, power), <strong>Qiang</strong> (strong, powerful), <strong>Yong</strong> (brave, courageous). Korean <strong>Yong</strong> (dragon, brave) and <strong>Dae</strong> (great, big).\"}}]\n2c:[\"$\",\"p\",\"10\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Sanskrit-derived strength names from India: <strong>Bala</strong> (strength), <strong>Veer/Vir</strong> (brave, heroic), <strong>Shakti</strong> (power, energy), <strong>Tejas</strong> (brilliance, power). These names carry spiritual depth alongside strength, making them meaningful choices for deeply bonded pets.\"}}]\n2d:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"11\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Nature-Inspired Strength Names 🌳\"]}]\n2e:[\"$\",\"p\",\"12\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Nature provides endless symbols of strength. <strong>Oakley/Oak</strong> from the mighty oak tree. <strong>Stone</strong>, <strong>Flint</strong>, <strong>Granite</strong> from unyielding rock. <strong>Steel</strong>, <strong>Iron</strong>, <strong>Titanium</strong> from metals. Animal-inspired strength: <strong>Bear</strong>, <strong>Lion</strong>, <strong>Tiger</strong>, <strong>Wolf</strong>, <strong>Hawk</strong>, <strong>Eagle</strong>, <strong>Bull</strong>, <strong>Gorilla</strong>.\"}}]\n2f:[\"$\",\"p\",\"13\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Weather phenomena bring dramatic strength: <strong>Storm</strong>, <strong>Thunder</strong>, <strong>Lightning</strong>, <strong>Cyclone</strong>, <strong>Avalanche</strong>, <strong>Tsunami</strong>, <strong>Quake</strong>. Mountain names evoke enduring power: <strong>Everest</strong>, <strong>Rocky</strong>, <strong>Summit</strong>, <strong>Ridge</strong>, <strong>Peak</strong>. For a more subtle strength, try <strong>River</strong> (relentless) or <strong>Cedar</strong> (tall and enduring).\"}}]\n30:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"14\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Warrior & Hero Strength Names 🛡️\"]}]\n31:[\"$\",\"p\",\"15\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Historical warriors and heroes provide some of the strongest name inspirations. <strong>Samson</strong> (biblical strongman), <strong>Achilles</strong> (Greek hero), <strong>Arthur</strong> (legendary king), <strong>Boudica</strong> (Celtic warrior queen), <strong>Leonidas</strong> (Spartan king), <strong>Alexander</strong> (conqueror).\"}}]\n32:[\"$\",\"p\",\"16\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Modern heroes: <strong>Ali</strong> (the Greatest), <strong>Tyson</strong> (Iron Mike), <strong>Diana</strong> (Wonder Woman), <strong>Thor</strong> (Marvel's god of thunder), <strong>Xena</strong> (warrior princess), <strong>Mulan</strong> (warrior woman). The name <strong>Brienne</strong> (from Game of Thrones) and <strong>Katniss</strong> (from Hunger Games) bring fictional warrior spirit.\"}}]\n33:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"❓ Frequently Asked Questions\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"details\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",nul